{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UG59xyKwrdNngbZt7xBthr","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've successfully read all five files. Here's the complete contents:\n\n## 1. SRD076 B2Sum Specification\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5493/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd076-b2sum.yaml`\n\nThe specification defines b2sum requirements:\n- Compute BLAKE2b-512 digests matching GNU gb2sum behavior\n- Support `--check` mode for verification with pass/fail output\n- Support `--binary`, `--text`, `--tag` output formats, and `--length` for variable digest length (bits, multiple of 8, max 512)\n- Handle SIGPIPE gracefully\n- Exit 0 on success, 1 on failure\n\nKey format details:\n- GNU text mode: \"HASH  FILENAME\"\n- GNU binary mode: \"HASH *FILENAME\"\n- BSD tag mode: \"BLAKE2b (FILENAME) = HASH\" (or \"BLAKE2b-256\" etc. when length is specified)\n- Stdin input uses \"HASH  -\"\n\n## 2. MD5Sum Reference Implementation\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5493/cmd/md5sum/main.go`\n\nSimple pattern showing:\n- Install SIGPIPE handler\n- Parse arguments for flags (--binary, --text, --tag, --check, --warn, --quiet, --status)\n- Create HashConfig with algorithm name, hash factory, and digest length\n- Call `hashutil.DigestFiles()` for normal mode or `hashutil.VerifyChecksums()` for check mode\n- Handle exit codes appropriately\n\n## 3. SHA256Sum Reference Implementation\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5493/cmd/sha256sum/main.go`\n\nExtended pattern with:\n- Additional `--zero` flag support (replace newlines with NUL)\n- Help and version text\n- Custom `nulWriter` wrapper for --zero output handling\n- Same hashutil integration pattern as md5sum\n\n## 4. HashUtil Core Package\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5493/pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go`\n\nProvides utility functions:\n- `ParseChecksumLine()`: Parses GNU or BSD format lines using regex\n- `VerifyChecksums()`: Reads checksum file, verifies entries, prints results\n- `DigestFiles()`: Computes and prints digests for files or stdin\n- `FormatGNU()`: GNU format output (text or binary mode)\n- `FormatBSDTag()`: BSD tag format output\n- `ComputeDigest()`: Computes hex-encoded digest from reader\n\nUses two regex patterns:\n- BSD tag: `^(\\S+) \\((.+)\\) = ([0-9a-fA-F]+)$`\n- GNU: `^([0-9a-fA-F]+) ([ *])(.+)$`\n\n## 5. HashConfig Type\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5493/pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go`\n\nKey types:\n- `HashConfig`: Algorithm name string, `NewHash` function, `DigestLen` int (expected full digest length in bytes)\n- `CheckOptions`: `Warn`, `Quiet`, `Status` bool flags\n\nThe pattern is clear: b2sum should follow the md5sum/sha256sum structure, creating a HashConfig with blake2b, then delegating to hashutil for the actual work."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b72c6101-4977-4320-bbcc-4a1c69190dc0","uuid":"22cd8bce-b6ef-41a8-bf9c-374363cdbd1b","timestamp":"2026-05-23T01:22:18.693Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to read several files from the go-unix-utils repository to understand the b2sum requirements and the pattern used by existing checksum utilities. Please read these files and return their full contents:\n\n1. docs/specs/software-requirements/srd076-b2sum.yaml — the SRD for b2sum\n2. cmd/md5sum/main.go — reference pattern for hashutil-based checksum utility\n3. cmd/sha256sum/main.go — second reference for checksum utility structure\n4. pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go — shared hash infrastructure\n5. pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go — HashConfig type\n\nThe working directory is /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5493","agentId":"a4a2dfdaef7dbc9c3","a