{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) requested implementation of Task #5493: creating `cmd/b2sum/main.go`, a BLAKE2b checksum utility for the go-unix-utils project. The task covers SRD076 requirements R1.1 (core BLAKE2b digest computation), R1.2 (stdin reading), R1.3 (output format), and R1.4 (binary/text mode flags). The utility must use `pkg/hashutil` for all digest computation and formatting, following the established pattern of `cmd/md5sum/main.go` and `cmd/sha256sum/main.go`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - BLAKE2b-512 hash algorithm (default 512-bit / 64-byte digest)\n   - `pkg/hashutil.HashConfig` struct: `{Algorithm string, NewHash func() hash.Hash, DigestLen int}`\n   - `pkg/hashutil.DigestFiles()` — handles file iteration, stdin (`-`), and output formatting\n   - `pkg/hashutil.FormatGNU()` — GNU format: `\"HASH  FILENAME\"` (text) or `\"HASH *FILENAME\"` (binary)\n   - `pkg/hashutil.FormatBSDTag()` — BSD tag format: `\"BLAKE2b (FILENAME) = HASH\"`\n   - `pkg/hashutil.ComputeDigest()` — computes hex-encoded digest from io.Reader\n   - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` — required at start of every cmd/ main()\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SPDX copyright header required on every Go file\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max (E9)\n   - Write-all-then-build strategy per go_style_constitution\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd076-b2sum.yaml** (read by agent)\n     - Defines BLAKE2b checksum utility requirements\n     - R1.1: Core digest computation using pkg/hashutil with BLAKE2b hash constructor\n     - R1.2: Read from stdin when no file args, using '-