or\n     - HashConfig with Algorithm \"BLAKE2b\", DigestLen 64 (512 bits / 8)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — no code has been written. The only action taken was research via the Explore agent.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Key concern: BLAKE2b is not in Go's standard library. It requires `golang.org/x/crypto/blake2b`. The project currently lists `golang.org/x/sys` as the only external dependency. Adding `golang.org/x/crypto` may require updating go.mod via `go get`. This is a necessary side effect since b2sum fundamentally requires BLAKE2b.\n   - The `blake2b.New512()` function returns `(hash.Hash, error)` — the error is always nil for the 512-bit variant, but the wrapper function for `NewHash func() hash.Hash` in HashConfig needs to handle this (likely wrapping it to ignore the nil error).\n   - The task scope is limited to R1.1-R1.4 only. Features like --check mode (R3.x, R4.x) and --length flag (R2.x) are NOT in scope, even though they appear in the full SRD.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The user provided a single massive message containing the full task specification including: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, package contracts, and constraints.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/b2sum/main.go` implementing SRD076 R1.1-R1.4\n   - Ensure `golang.org/x/crypto/blake2b` dependency is available (may need `go get`)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/b2sum ./cmd/b2sum/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/b2sum/` to verify no warnings (AC2)\n   - Test that `bin/b2sum <file>` produces correct BLAKE2b digest output (AC3)\n   - Test that `echo test | bin/b2sum` reads from stdin (AC4)\n   - Test that --binary and --text flags are accepted and work (AC5)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The Ex